media: iris: wrap timestamp metadata index before capture completion

metadata_idx is incremented after storing each input buffer, but previously
wrapped only when the next input arrived. A capture completion with no matching
timestamp in that interval uses metadata_idx directly in iris_get_ts_metadata.
After the 32nd input this reads beyond tss[32]. UBSAN reports both fallback
accesses in iris_buffer.c during repeated 4K H.264 decoding.

Wrap immediately after advancing so the fallback index remains in bounds.
Retain the existing defensive check before storing metadata. This preserves
the current next-slot fallback policy; selecting different timestamp metadata
is a separate semantic change.

This is a candidate kernel patch, not installed on the test host.

--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_common.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_common.c
@@ -44,6 +44,8 @@
 	inst->tss[inst->metadata_idx].ts_ns = vb->timestamp;
 
 	inst->metadata_idx++;
+	if (inst->metadata_idx == ARRAY_SIZE(inst->tss))
+		inst->metadata_idx = 0;
 }
 
 int iris_process_streamon_input(struct iris_inst *inst)
